  "query_preview": "..For much of the next 7 days southeast Arizona \nwill be in a favorable easterly monsoon flow pattern that will \nkeep daily chances of showers and thunderstorms in the forecast \nfor much of the area with day-to-day variability in coverage of\nstorms. There will be the continued daily hazards of severe wind\ngusts, blowing dust and flash flooding. WPC is highlighting \nMonday and possibly Wednesday for enhanced chances for increased\nflash flooding threat. Not everyone will get rain every day \nwhich is the monsoon in a nutshell. High temperatures today and \ntomorrow will be on the hot side with a few spots near record \nhighs and HeatRisk in Moderate to Major categories. Highs next\nweek will be around normal.\n\nAt 245 am satellite imagery showed partly to mostly cloudy \nskies with a small MCS decaying across NE Sonora MX, or south of\nCochise county. Radar showed isolated showers and thunderstorms\nmain west and south of Tucson with outflow boundaries running \naround producing gusts up to 35 mph. \n\nFor today, after the clouds diminish this morning, the main \narea for widely scattered thunderstorms development later this\nafternoon into this evening will be west of a Dudleyville to \nNogales line. There are a few CAMs that bring an increased\nthreat for isolated severe thunderstorms, blowing dust and \nbrief heavy rain to the western parts of Pima county after 6 pm.\nConfidence low at this time but something that will be watched.",
